# IG-2026-027 — ADT Data Breach

> **Organization:** ADT Inc.  
> **Incident ID:** IG-2026-027  
> **Month:** April 2026  
> **Region:** United States  
> **Industry:** Security / Home Services  
> **Incident Type:** Unauthorized Access / Data Breach / Extortion  
> **Affected Scale:** ~5.5 million unique email addresses in published breach data  
> **Threat Actor:** ShinyHunters — publicly attributed / reported  
> **Initial Access:** Not publicly established by ADT  
> **Status:** CONFIRMED  
> **Severity:** CRITICAL  

---

## Overview

ADT confirmed a cybersecurity incident after detecting unauthorized access to certain cloud-based environments on April 20, 2026.

The affected environments contained information belonging to customers and prospective customers.

ADT stated that exposed information primarily included:

- Names
- Telephone numbers
- Physical addresses

A smaller percentage of affected records also contained:

- Dates of birth
- Last four digits of Social Security numbers
- Last four digits of Tax IDs

Data subsequently associated with the incident was indexed by Have I Been Pwned at approximately **5.5 million unique email addresses**.

ADT stated that:

- Payment information was not accessed.
- Customer security systems were not affected or compromised.

This distinction is critical.

The incident was a significant compromise of customer information, but available evidence does not establish compromise of ADT alarm or customer-security infrastructure.

